{
  "theorem_name": "OAI.PiExponent.tendsto_log_div_of_normalized_pow",
  "theorem_title": "Sublinear logarithmic growth from positive normalized power growth",
  "natural_language_statement": "Let f : ℝ → ℝ, d : ℕ, and L : ℝ. If f(H) / H^d tends to L as H tends to +∞ and L > 0, then Real.log(f(H)) / H tends to 0 as H tends to +∞.",
  "tags": [
    "asymptotic-analysis",
    "number-theory",
    "openai-pi-exponent-017"
  ],
  "explanation": "The positive limit ensures f(H) / H^d is eventually positive, hence f(H) is positive for all sufficiently large H. The logarithm splits as log(f(H) / H^d) + d log(H); the first term has a finite limit and becomes negligible after division by H, while log(H) / H tends to zero.",
